.TH STARDUST 1 "16 September 2026" "Stardust" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
stardust \- manage Backdrop platforms and sites from the shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stardust
.RB [ \-n ]
.I command
.RI [ args... ]
.PP
.B stardust
.BR \-h | \-\-help | help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stardust
is the command-line control plane for Backdrop CMS on
.B Stardust
and the VPS.
It is the piece that replaces Drupal Aegir / BOA
.I without
a PHP hosting panel.
.PP
Think of three layers:
.IP \(bu 3
A
.B platform
is one Backdrop codebase under
.B /srv/platforms/NAME
(Git tree, shared core, modules, themes).
.IP \(bu 3
A
.B product
(also called a site) is one website inside that tree:
its own database, files, and config.
Example: platform
.B ecom
holds products
.B thq
and
.B kl .
.IP \(bu 3
An
.B environment
is which machine and Git branch you are on:
.B devel
(devel host or a laptop),
.B test
or
.B live
(VPS).
.PP
.B stardust
creates platforms and products, wires Bee and
.BR crdir (1),
writes the Apache name, and creates the MariaDB user.
Day-to-day content and config still go through
.BR bee (1)
with
.B \-\-root
and
.B \-\-site .
.PP
Do
.I not
type
.B sudo stardust
(exit 2).
Log in as the operator account
(or
.BR deploy )
and run the wrapper.
Root work goes through
.B /usr/local/sbin/stardust-priv
only
(path allowlist under
.B /srv/platforms
and
.BR /srv/stardust ,
DB names
.BR bd_* ).
.PP
The daily operator
(the login that ran
.B stardust-install.sh ,
or
.B \-H NAME )
must be in groups
.B www-admin
and
.BR stardust .
After
.B usermod \-aG
use
.B exec su \- $USER
.
.B exec bash
does
.I not
refresh groups.
.PP
PHP-writable trees are
.B www-data:www-admin
plus default POSIX ACLs.
Secrets are
.B deploy:stardust
mode 0640
(Apache is
.I not
in
.BR stardust ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
Dry run.
Print each action with a leading
.B +
and change nothing.
Use this the first time you run any mutating command.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " help
Print the same new-admin help that is in this manual's
.B EXAMPLES
section.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS doctor
Check that this box is ready:
users
.BR deploy ,
.BR www-admin ,
and the operator login
.RB ( \-H
or the user who ran the installer);
groups
.B www-admin
and
.BR stardust ;
.B stardust-priv
and
.BR setfacl ;
directories under
.B /srv/stardust
and
.BR /srv/platforms ,
and that
.BR bee ,
.BR crdir ,
Apache, PHP, and MariaDB are on PATH.
CSF and WireGuard are notes, not failures.
.SS list
Walk
.B /srv/platforms
and print each platform, its Git branch, and the product folders
that already have settings.
.SS env
Print the values loaded from
.B ~/.stardust.conf
or
.BR /etc/stardust.conf .
Useful when a command used the wrong role or path.
.SS platform-add NAME
Create
.BI /srv/platforms/ NAME \fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-git " URL"
Clone that Git remote (Gitea).
.TP
.BI \-\-branch " BRANCH"
Branch to check out after clone.
Default: the role in
.B STARDUST_ROLE
(usually
.BR devel ).
.PP
With no
.B \-\-git ,
.B bee dl-core web
builds a fresh Backdrop tree.
If the directory already exists, the command stops and leaves it alone.
.SS site-add PLATFORM PRODUCT
Add one product inside an existing platform.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
Hostname Apache and Backdrop should answer
(default:
.BI PRODUCT . ROLE \fR,
for example
.BR www.devel ).
.TP
.BI \-\-name " TITLE"
Site name passed to
.B bee install
(default:
.IB PRODUCT " " ROLE \fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-pass " PASS"
MariaDB password.
If omitted, a random password is stored in
.B /srv/stardust/state/secrets/PLATFORM/PRODUCT
and
.B PRODUCT.cnf
(not printed).
MariaDB create reads the
.B .cnf
so the password is not on
.BR argv .
.PP
What
.B site-add
does, in order:
.IP 1. 4
.B crdir \-s \-o www-data \-g www-admin
on
.BR files/PRODUCT ,
.BR files_private/PRODUCT ,
.B config/PRODUCT/active
.IP 2. 4
.B crdir
(no
.BR \-s )
on
.B config/PRODUCT/staging
.IP 3. 4
Copy and patch
.B web/sites/PRODUCT/settings.php
with the Backdrop path overrides
.IP 4. 4
Append
.B $sites['HOST'] = 'PRODUCT'
to
.B web/sites/sites.php
.IP 5. 4
Write
.B settings.local.php
(database DSN + trusted host).
An existing file is
.I not
overwritten.
.IP 6. 4
.B CREATE DATABASE
and
.B CREATE USER
on localhost only.
Name:
.BI bd_ PRODUCT _ ROLE
.IP 7. 4
.B bee \-\-root=.../web \-\-site=PRODUCT install \-\-auto
.IP 8. 4
Create or extend
.BI /etc/apache2/sites-available/ PLATFORM \- ROLE .conf
and reload Apache
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/stardust.conf
System defaults written by
.BR stardust-install.sh .
.TP
.B /etc/php/*/fpm/conf.d/35-stardust-harden.ini
FPM and apache2 only.
.B disable_functions
(passthru, popen, proc_*, dl, pcntl_*),
live/test
.B opcache.validate_timestamps=0 .
Not applied to CLI.
.TP
.B /etc/php/*/cli/conf.d/35-stardust-cli.ini
CLI only. No
.BR disable_functions
so
.B bee
still works.
.TP
.B /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52stardust-unattended
Security updates only;
.B Automatic-Reboot
is
.BR false .
.TP
.B /etc/msmtprc
You write this after install so
.B NOTIFY=
can send mail via
.BR msmtp-mta .
.PP
Host packages the installer pulls on Devuan/Debian include
.BR apache2-utils ,
.BR php-intl ,
.BR php-bcmath ,
.BR php-imagick ,
.BR php-apcu ,
.BR mariadb-backup ,
.BR logwatch ,
.BR goaccess ,
.BR etckeeper ,
.BR smartmontools ,
.BR irqbalance ,
.BR haveged ,
.BR moreutils ,
.BR jq ,
.BR pv ,
and
.BR age .
.TP
.B ~/.stardust.conf
Per-user override
.RB ( deploy
and
.BR www-admin ).
.TP
.B /srv/stardust
Control plane: backups, state, extra binaries.
.TP
.B /srv/platforms
Backdrop checkouts.
Never run devel, test, and live out of one working copy.
.TP
.B /etc/csf/csf.conf
Optional CSF policy from
.B stardust-install.sh \-F .
SSH is not world-open; use WireGuard
.B 10.8.0.0/24
or LAN
.BR 192.168.1.0/24 .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STARDUST_CONF
If set, load this file instead of the usual conf search.
.TP
.B STARDUST_ROLE
.BR devel ", " test ", or " live .
Picks default branch, default hostname suffix, and database suffix.
.SH FIRST HOUR ON A NEW BOX
.IP 1. 4
Copy the artifacts folder onto the machine
.RI ( crdir ,
.BR stardust ,
.B stardust-install.sh
must sit next to each other).
.IP 2. 4
Preview, then install the host:
.PP
.RS
laptop:
.B ./stardust-install.sh \-n \-\-localhost
.PP
devel host:
.B ./stardust-install.sh \-n \-m devel
.PP
VPS:
.B ./stardust-install.sh \-n \-m test
(or
.BR \-m live )
.RE
.IP 3. 4
Run the same command without
.BR \-n .
Set passwords:
.B sudo passwd deploy
,
.B sudo passwd www-admin
, and
.B sudo passwd
on the operator login
then
.B exec su \- $USER
.IP 4. 4
.B stardust doctor
must print READY.
.IP 5. 4
Add a platform, then each product, always with
.B \-n
first.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS See whether this machine is ready
.nf
stardust doctor
stardust env
stardust list
.fi
.SS Dry-run a new empty platform (no Git yet)
.nf
stardust \-n platform-add scratch
stardust platform-add scratch
.fi
.PP
Bee downloads Backdrop core into
.BR /srv/platforms/scratch/web .
.SS Clone ecom from Gitea onto the devel host (devel)
.nf
stardust \-n platform-add mysite \e
  \-\-git git@git.example:org/mysite.git \e
  \-\-branch devel
stardust platform-add mysite \e
  \-\-git git@git.example:org/mysite.git \e
  \-\-branch devel
.fi
.SS Add the two ecom products on the devel host
.nf
stardust \-n site-add mysite www \-\-host www.devel \-\-name "THQ devel"
stardust site-add mysite www \-\-host www.devel \-\-name "THQ devel"
stardust site-add mysite shop  \-\-host shop.devel  \-\-name "KL devel"
.fi
.PP
Open
.B http://www.devel
and
.B http://shop.devel
(dnsmasq on the devel host and on
.B \-\-localhost
maps
.B *.devel
for you).
.SS Same products on the VPS test checkout
The VPS uses a
.I second
working copy, not the devel host tree.
.nf
# on the VPS, role=test in /etc/stardust.conf
stardust platform-add mysite-test \e
  \-\-git git@git.example:org/mysite.git \e
  \-\-branch test
stardust site-add mysite-test thq \-\-host www.test.example
stardust site-add mysite-test kl  \-\-host shop.test.example
.fi
.SS Live hostnames
.nf
stardust site-add mysite-live thq \-\-host www.example.com
stardust site-add mysite-live kl  \-\-host shop.example.com
.fi
.PP
Cloudflare in front of the VPS: Flexible origin is HTTP only.
Full (strict) needs an origin certificate; that is not
.B site-add .
.SS After the site exists \- Bee, not Stardust
.nf
bee \-\-root=/srv/platforms/mysite/web \-\-site=thq status
bee \-\-root=/srv/platforms/mysite/web \-\-site=thq cc all
bee \-\-root=/srv/platforms/mysite/web \-\-site=thq config-export
bee \-\-root=/srv/platforms/mysite/web \-\-site=kl  updb
.fi
.PP
A Bee command without
.B \-\-site
on a multisite tree may pick the wrong product.
.SS Feature worktree on the devel host
.B newfeature
is a separate tool.
From a site root:
.nf
cd /srv/platforms/mysite/web/sites/www
newfeature maps
.fi
.SS Backup, restore, clone, smoke check
.nf
stardust \-n site-backup mysite www
stardust site-backup mysite www
stardust site-restore mysite www
stardust site-restore \-\-from /srv/stardust/backups/mysite/www/devel/20260916-210000 mysite www
stardust site-clone mysite www mysite www-copy \-\-host www-copy.devel
stardust site-check mysite www \-\-host www.devel
stardust backup-all
.fi
.SS Upgrade and promote (VPS)
.nf
# devel host: commit + push devel, merge to test on Gitea
# VPS:
stardust \-n promote mysite \-\-to test
stardust promote mysite \-\-to test
stardust promote mysite \-\-to live
stardust platform-upgrade mysite-test
stardust log 20
stardust last
.fi
.PP
.B promote
refuses to run when
.B STARDUST_ROLE
is
.BR devel .
Fast-forward only; a diverged branch is an error, not a merge.
.SS Maintenance and cron
.nf
stardust site-disable mysite www
stardust site-enable mysite www
stardust \-n cron-all
.fi
.PP
The installer writes
.B /etc/cron.d/stardust
(nightly
.B backup-all
at 03:15, Bee cron four times an hour).
.SS Stardust itself as a Gitea repo (laptop first)
The CLI is its own private repo. It is not a Backdrop platform.
Do not
.B platform-add stardust .
.nf
# Gitea UI: ORG/stardust, empty, private
cd /path/to/artifacts
git init && git checkout -B devel
git add stardust-install.sh stardust stardust.1 stardust-lib \e
  crdir crdir.1 newfeature stardust-tutorial.txt .gitignore
git commit -m "stardust CLI"
git remote add origin git@git.example:org/stardust.git
git remote -v
ssh -T git@git.example
git push -u origin devel
# later from this laptop:
git push
# same as: git push origin devel
.fi
.PP
On the devel host or the VPS:
.nf
git clone -b devel git@git.example:org/stardust.git /home/deploy/stardust
cd /home/deploy/stardust
./stardust-install.sh \-n \-m devel
.fi
.SS Host install variants
.nf
# laptop, 127.0.0.1 only, dnsmasq on, no CSF, no certbot
./stardust-install.sh \-n \-\-localhost
./stardust-install.sh \-\-localhost
.fi
.nf
# devel host devel + optional CSF (SSH only via WireGuard / LAN)
./stardust-install.sh \-n \-m devel
./stardust-install.sh \-F \-m devel
.fi
.nf
# VPS: no dnsmasq (public DNS), certbot yes
./stardust-install.sh \-n \-m test
./stardust-install.sh \-F \-m live
.fi
.SH WORDS YOU WILL SEE
.TP
.B deploy
Unix account that owns Git trees and runs Bee.
.TP
.B www-admin
Human login that can write the same 0770 trees.
.TP
.B www-data
Apache/PHP daemon group.
.TP
.B Bee
Backdrop's Drush replacement.
Always
.B \-\-root=/srv/platforms/PLATFORM/web \-\-site=PRODUCT .
.TP
.B crdir
Creates files/config dirs as
.B deploy:www-data
mode 0770.
.B \-s
is setgid for files that PHP also writes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.B doctor
prints READY.
.B site-check
prints OK.
.TP
.B 1
Understood the arguments but could not finish:
missing platform or product, Bee/git/MariaDB failure,
dirty tree or diverged branch on
.BR promote ,
failed
.B site-check
after upgrade,
lock already held,
or
.B doctor
NOT READY.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown flag, missing argument,
.B \-\-to devel ,
or
.B promote
on a host whose role is
.BR devel .
.PP
Mutating commands also write
.B rc=
on the last line of
.B stardust last .
.SH BUGS
.B site-delete
is still not implemented.
A failed
.B site-check
after upgrade does not auto-restore; use
.B site-restore
by hand.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crdir (1),
.BR bee (1),
.BR apache2 (8),
.B stardust-install.sh
.PP
Tutorials in the artifacts folder:
.BR stardust-tutorial.txt ,
.BR ecom-multisite-tutorial.txt ,
.BR mysite-test-live-filesystem-tutorial.docx .
.SH AUTHOR
Written for the Stardust Backdrop platforms layout.
